tools.description:
LinkedIn & email outreach

Read your most recently received emails from your connected mailbox inbox (Gmail / Outlook / SMTP; read-only). Use this for requests like 'get my last N emails', 'check my inbox', or 'show my recent replies'. Bounces are flagged. account_id is optional when only one mailbox is connected; if the user names a specific mailbox (e.g. 'my gmail'), call linkupapi_list_accounts and pass the matching account_id. Pass unread_only to return only unread messages. This tool is part of plugin `LinkupAPI`.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__linkupapi_channel_get_emails(args: {
  // Email mailbox account_id (from linkupapi_list_accounts). Optional when a single mailbox is connected.
  account_id?: string;
  // Max emails to return (e.g. 5).
  limit?: number;
  unread_only?: boolean;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

LinkedIn & email outreach

Profile & company lookups on a connected channel (read-only; LinkedIn today). Pick an `action` and pass the matching `params`:
- get_me: no params — returns your own profile.
- get: { profile_url | identifier, profile_urn? } — full public profile.
- get_contact: { profile_url } — contact info (email, phone if visible).
- search_people: { keyword?, location?, current_company?, company_url?, first_name?, last_name?, title?, industry?, school_url?, network?, offset?, limit? }.
- search_companies: { keyword?, location?, sector?, company_size?, offset?, limit? }.
- get_company: { company_url } — full company page data.
- get_candidates: { job_id, total_results? } — applicants for a job (recruiter).
- get_viewers: { count?, offset? } — who viewed your profile.
- get_reactions: { profile_url, count?, cursor? } — reactions on a profile's posts.
- get_comments: { profile_url, count?, cursor? } — comments authored by a profile. This tool is part of plugin `LinkupAPI`.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__linkupapi_channel_get_profile(args: {
  // Channel account_id from linkupapi_login.
  account_id: string;
  action: "get_me" | "get" | "get_contact" | "search_people" | "search_companies" | "get_company" | "get_candidates" | "get_viewers" | "get_reactions" | "get_comments";
  // Action-specific params. See description.
  params?: { [key: string]: unknown; };
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

LinkedIn & email outreach

Send an email from your connected mailbox (Gmail / Outlook / SMTP). Delivered immediately from your mailbox and cannot be unsent. Body: pass `text` (plain text — often the best-delivering format for cold outreach), `html`, or both. account_id is optional when only one mailbox is connected; if the user names a specific mailbox (e.g. 'from my gmail'), call linkupapi_list_accounts and pass the matching account_id. This tool is part of plugin `LinkupAPI`.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__linkupapi_channel_send_email(args: {
  // Email mailbox account_id (from linkupapi_list_accounts). Optional when a single mailbox is connected.
  account_id?: string;
  // HTML body (optional).
  html?: string;
  // Optional Reply-To address.
  reply_to?: string;
  subject: string;
  // Plain-text body.
  text?: string;
  // Recipient email address.
  to: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

LinkedIn & email outreach

Public-data enrichment & email tools. No account_id required — uses LinkupAPI's managed pipeline. Pick an `action` and provide the matching `params`:
- enrich_person: { first_name, last_name, company_name } — finds the LinkedIn URL and returns the full profile.
- enrich_company: { company_domain | company_url } — company info from a domain or URL.
- find_email: { linkedin_url } OR { first_name, last_name, company_name | company_domain } — professional email finder.
- validate_email: { email } — SMTP, MX & catch-all check.
- reverse_email: { email } — finds the person behind a professional email (personal providers like gmail/yahoo are rejected).
- search_jobs: { keywords, location?, country?, limit?, is_remote?, job_type? } — job board postings (Indeed/LinkedIn/Glassdoor). country drives the Indeed/Glassdoor region; if omitted it is inferred from location (e.g. 'Madrid, Spain' → spain), else defaults to france. job_type ∈ fulltime|parttime|contract|internship.
- extract_employees: { company_url, limit? } — employees of a company (LinkedIn search).
Cost: 1 credit per call. This tool is part of plugin `LinkupAPI`.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__linkupapi_linkupapi_enrich(args: {
  action: "enrich_person" | "enrich_company" | "find_email" | "validate_email" | "reverse_email" | "search_jobs" | "extract_employees";
  // Action-specific params. See description.
  params?: { [key: string]: unknown; };
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

LinkedIn & email outreach

Get full details of one account (status, country, webhook_url, timestamps). This tool is part of plugin `LinkupAPI`.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__linkupapi_linkupapi_get_account(args: {
  // Account identifier.
  account_id: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

LinkedIn & email outreach

List API call logs for the authenticated user. Filter by action (e.g. 'send', 'invite'), account_id, or status ('success' / 'error'). This tool is part of plugin `LinkupAPI`.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__linkupapi_linkupapi_get_logs(args: {
  // Filter by account.
  account_id?: string;
  // Filter by action name.
  action?: string;
  // Page size (1-200, default 50).
  limit?: number;
  // Pagination offset (default 0).
  offset?: number;
  status?: "success" | "error" | "checkpoint";
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

LinkedIn & email outreach

Aggregated API usage over the full history: total calls and credits, plus per-account and per-action breakdowns (calls, successes, errors, credits). Pass account_id to get the per-action detail of one account. Optional ISO date range (date_from / date_to, YYYY-MM-DD, date_to inclusive). This tool is part of plugin `LinkupAPI`.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__linkupapi_linkupapi_get_usage_stats(args: {
  // Scope every figure to this account.
  account_id?: string;
  // ISO date, calls at or after.
  date_from?: string;
  // ISO date, inclusive.
  date_to?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

LinkedIn & email outreach

List every channel account connected to your API key — each with its account_id, platform (linkedin/email), mailbox address, provider (gmail/outlook), and status. Call this to pick the right account_id when the user names a specific account or mailbox (e.g. 'my gmail'). A LinkedIn account with a Recruiter seat carries its id in `recruiter.account_id`: that is the account_id linkedin_recruiter_seat takes. This tool is part of plugin `LinkupAPI`.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__linkupapi_linkupapi_list_accounts(args: {
  // Also list Recruiter seat accounts as their own entries (kind recruiter_seat).
  include_seats?: boolean;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```
